# dependencies
node_modules/
# ...and `node_modules` WITHOUT the trailing slash, which is not redundant.
# A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY. A *symlink* named `node_modules`
# is not a directory, so it slipped past the rule above and was staged by a
# `git add -A` during a conflict resolution -- committing a self-referential
# symlink (`apps/web/node_modules` -> its own absolute path) to `main`, where
# it broke `npx` locally for anyone who cloned it. The root `.gitignore`
# carries a comment about the same class of accident. Both spellings, so
# neither shape can be staged again.
node_modules

# build output
dist/
dist-ssr/

# local env / logs
*.local
*.log

# editor / os
.DS_Store
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# vite / vitest caches
.vite/
coverage/
.vercel
.env*

# playwright (e2e browser/a11y baseline) — run artifacts only.
# The specs, config and a11y baseline under e2e/ ARE committed; nothing below
# is. These directories hold traces, videos, screenshots and downloaded browser
# state, i.e. binaries that must never enter the repository.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
playwright/.cache/
